{"term":"Ottawa","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c246a1284589f403a6","definition":"A city in Ontario, Canada; the capital city of Canada.","example":"And of course, in July 1967 De Gaulle did come to Canada. He made his speeches in Quebec, was enthusiastically received on the Chemin du Roy, shouted “Vive le Quebec libre” in Montreal and, on learning of the reaction of the Canadian government, returned to Paris without going to Ottawa.","pos":"name","synonyms":["National Capital Region","NCR","Ottawa-Hull","Ottawa-Gatineau","O-town"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mega-Ottawa","Ottawa County","Ottawa-Gatineau","Ottawa-Hull","Ottawian"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ottawa#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:22d3cf9edcea7e17c4","definition":"A river flowing southeast between Ontario and Quebec, Canada into the St. Lawrence River.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":["Kichi Sipi","Kitchissippi"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mega-Ottawa","Ottawa County","Ottawa-Gatineau","Ottawa-Hull","Ottawian"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ottawa#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6de67fc9e3151c5fc9","definition":"A number of places in the United States:","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":["National Capital Region","NCR","Ottawa-Hull","Ottawa-Gatineau","O-town"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mega-Ottawa","Ottawa County","Ottawa-Gatineau","Ottawa-Hull","Ottawian"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ottawa#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e9a4b3708fe1c4c29b","definition":"A village and former commune of Ivory Coa